  "body": "Add the single shared React/TypeScript/Vite browser foundation for the driver/contact lanes: one shell/router/language provider, source-owned controls and fact/state primitives, generic noindex metadata, approved brand assets and a token-free session UI bridge. Feature screens remain unavailable until their owners supply components; the default access state is explicitly unconfigured.\n\nFrozen head: `e154a6d7fc987c656395503a1ef794a0e3de64fd`. Inspected backend base: `ebc8fb1d36f441ef012ca585201cefabf61383d6`; this PR targets `codex/aws-durable-backend`. Backend root package/lock, source and CI are unchanged. Earlier source revisions and raw evidence remain preserved.\n\nResolve all three findings from independent review5560715902: validate the route identity before assigning its tab title, give the actual brand-home anchor a44px minimum target, and match the unconfigured API boundary by pathname so `/v1?query` returns503JSON. Configured proxy forwarding retains the query unchanged. Q52's original b1134025 regression source is untouched:9pass/4fail before,13pass/0fail on this exact revision. Node24.17 strict typecheck/build and all9 foundation tests pass, including extended real production-preview socket tests. The affected-axis native browser matrix retains80 full-page captures across five viewports, both locales, four route states and dev/production preview; heading/title match, no overflow/runtime exception and minimum actual brand target44px. Six additional HTTP controls return the expected503JSON. Original-reviewer confirmation is requested; author checks are not independent acceptance.\n\nBoth dev and production preview proxy only to an explicit credential-free loopback API target; absent configuration returns no-store JSON503. The production build strips development fixture entries and the optional local test mount hook. Credentials are not stored by this foundation. Hairline0.5.1 is pinned but not imported into the base bundle. Six RGBA brand images and the three-entry favicon were verified; metadata contains no participant, coordinate or route identifiers.\n\nThe source detector reports no findings and rejects its planted layout control. URL mode could not scan because Puppeteer is missing; its zero exit is not a pass. Full Git-bound UI proof remains RED for independent/aggregate feature and interaction coverage. API/session45, driver50, contact/privacy51, runtime44/46 and optional visual53\u201356 work remain separate. Whole-app production composition is a subsequent branch; actual server authentication, complete driver/contact journeys, physical/human/provider evidence and deployment are not established by this foundation. No merges or real sends; only44 integrates after actionable reviews are resolved.\n\nRefs #2\nRefs #3\n",
